# Git hooks and shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# On Windows, autocrlf rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, and Git for Windows'
# sh then fails on the shebang with a "bad interpreter" error that names a
# carriage return — an obscure failure for something that looks like a plain
# text file. Forcing LF here means the hooks work on a fresh Windows clone.
hooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
